<BaseLayout title="About Percentage Increase Calculator" description="Learn why Percentage Increase Calculator was created, what it calculates, and how the site approaches clear percentage explanations." active="about">
  <header class="page-head wrap"><h1>About this calculator</h1><p>A focused reference tool for everyday before-and-after percentage questions.</p></header>
  <section class="content-page"><div class="content-grid wrap"><article class="prose">
    <h2>One job, explained clearly</h2>
    <p>Percentage Increase Calculator helps people compare two values, apply a known increase, or work backward to an original number. It is designed for general arithmetic involving prices, salaries, counts, measurements, and other everyday quantities.</p>
    <p>The calculator shows more than a final percentage. It also provides the difference, multiplier, and working so readers can understand the result.</p>
    <h2>Written for a general US audience</h2>
    <p>Examples use familiar US number and currency formats. The formulas themselves are not country-specific. Important decisions involving tax, contracts, investments, employment, or official reporting should be checked against the relevant rules.</p>
    <h2>Who writes the site</h2>
    <p>The guides are written by <a href="/author/nikita-mondal/">Nikita Mondal</a>. Each explanation starts from its own question and includes a worked calculation rather than relying on unsupported claims.</p>
